  "htmlContent": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><title>You are allowed to change your mind</title><style>@media only screen and (max-width:620px){.letter{padding-left:24px!important;padding-right:24px!important}.title{font-size:32px!important}.outer{padding:16px 8px!important}}</style></head>\n<body style=\"margin:0;background:#e8dedf;color:#302731\"><div style=\"display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;opacity:0;mso-hide:all\">A writing practice for revisiting an impression without judging yourself.</div>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"background:#e8dedf\"><tr><td class=\"outer\" align=\"center\" style=\"padding:40px 16px\">\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"600\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:600px;background:#fcf9f4;border-collapse:collapse\">\n<tr><td style=\"height:6px;background:#653c56;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"letter\" style=\"padding:40px 48px 24px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font:11px Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:2px;color:#744b65\">WRITING · TAROT · SPIRITUAL REFLECTION</p><p style=\"margin:0;font:32px/1.2 Georgia,serif;color:#302731\">Letters from Kali</p><div style=\"height:1px;background:#d9ccd2;margin:24px 0 28px\"></div><p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font:11px Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:2px;color:#744b65\">ON DISCERNMENT · LETTER 04</p><h1 class=\"title\" style=\"margin:0;font:normal 38px/1.15 Georgia,serif;color:#653c56\">You are allowed to change your mind.</h1></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"letter\" style=\"padding:0 48px 40px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">What happens when an impression you felt strongly about doesn’t hold up?</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">It can be tempting to defend it, explain it away, or decide you can never trust yourself again.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">There is another possibility: let the experience teach you something.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">Discernment leaves room for new information. You can take an impression seriously, examine it, and change your understanding. None of those steps requires you to turn against yourself.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">Writing gives you something more useful than a verdict about whether you were right. It gives you a record of what you noticed and what you learned.</p><table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"margin:26px 0;background:#efe5d6;border-left:3px solid #744b65\"><tr><td style=\"padding:24px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;font:11px Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:2px;color:#744b65\">A MOMENT ON THE PAGE</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">Return to one impression you wrote down earlier:</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">What did I notice at the time?</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">What did I assume it meant?</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">What happened, and what is still unknown?</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">What would I understand differently now?</p></td></tr></table><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">You may find that you noticed something real and gave it the wrong meaning. You may find that a hope or fear shaped your interpretation. You may simply need more time to know.</p><p style=\"margin:28px 0;font:italic 26px/1.4 Georgia,serif;color:#653c56\">Trust can include the freedom to reconsider.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">For this week, try replacing ‘I should have known’ with ‘What can I learn from this?’</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">What becomes possible when you give yourself permission to revise an impression? You’re welcome to reply.</p><p style=\"margin:30px 0 0;font:italic 30px Georgia,serif;color:#653c56\">Kali</p></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"letter\" style=\"padding:26px 48px;background:#f5f0e8;border-top:1px solid #d9ccd2;text-align:center;font:12px/1.8 Arial,sans-serif;color:#655b61\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\">Randi Agency</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\">11265 Hallett Street, Soddy Daisy, TN 37379</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\">You&#x27;ve received it because you&#x27;ve subscribed to our newsletter.</p><p style=\"margin:12px 0 0\"><a href=\"{{ unsubscribe }}\" style=\"color:#653c56;text-decoration:underline\">Unsubscribe</a></p></td></tr>\n</table></td></tr></table></body></html>",
